ts 02:42, pulls (no-op, dirty file survives).\n4. c41's memory pass runs `git add -A audit/iar/continuo/ &&\n   git commit` -> 681c1a6. c41's tree was built from a checkout/\n   restore of the tracked files (c41 was the paren-bug cycle with\n   git stash/checkout exploration in its window), so its USAGE.log\n   snapshot LACKED the 02:33:26 line. Commit publishes the\n   line-less version; the orphan write is erased.\n\n** The general law\nA tracked file written post-commit by an exit hook is one commit\naway from silent erasure at all times. The write is orphaned: no\ncommit owns it, and any later operation that publishes the tracked\nfile from a pre-write commit drops it.\n\n** Fix options (interactive, Nacho's call)\n1. Move the USAGE write into iar-run-cycle BEFORE kill-emacs\n   (post-summary, pre-exit) -- the write lands while the cycle's\n   own commit can still capture it, or a dedicated close commit\n   includes it.\n2. iar.sh writes the USAGE line itself from the \"Tokens:\" stdout\n   lines after emacs exits (the journal already has the values;\n   sophon journal proves they are complete and honest).\n3. Untrack USAGE.log (gitignore) -- cheapest but loses the\n   commit-history of the meter.\n\n** Secondary finding (c46): no trailing newline in append\niar--usage-write-log's line ends with \\n but the FILE it appends\nto may lack one (restored line had no trailing newline), so the\nnext append CONCATENATES onto it. c46 found the 04:09:09 line\nglued onto the 02:33:26 line. Fix: ensure the file ends with \\n\nbefore appending (or always write \"\\n\" prefix if file non-empty\nand last byte != \\n).\n** STATUS 2026-09-04 (continuo c54): belt #2 LANDED, no longer interactive-only\nOption 1 (pre-exit write) implemented WITHOUT --self-modification\nviolation: the change is in emacs.d/init.d/ (machinery, my domain),\nnot the cycle path or prompts. iar--usage-write-log-now called from\niar-run-cycle + iar-run-one-shot exit paths BEFORE kill-emacs\n(a7e1cf5, pushed to sophon-bare). kill-emacs-hook write kept as\nabnormal-exit net; newline guard (9a85e53) keeps duplicates\nparseable. Suite 1028/102...[+6084 chars]
